WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.500
South Korea occupies the southern Korean Peninsula, balancing dynastic palaces and digital culture.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:11.000
Hallasan, a dormant shield volcano on Jeju Island, rises to 1,947 meters as the highest summit.

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:17.000
King Sejong the Great created the scientific Hangul alphabet in 1443 to empower all citizens.

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:23.000
Traditional Hanbok is distinguished by vibrant Jeogori jackets and sweeping Chima skirts.

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:29.000
Heritage music includes Gayageum 12-string zithers and Samulnori percussion quartets.

